      "path": "book-list.html",
      "language": "markup",
      "code": "<!-- Paste into a Code Block element (Render as code: OFF). It lists the books from this\n     site's own REST API, so it keeps working wherever the page is moved. -->\n<div id=\"book-list\" class=\"book-list\" aria-live=\"polite\">Loading books…</div>\n\n<style>\n  .book-list { display: grid; gap: 24px; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(180px, 1fr)); }\n  .book-list a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }\n  .book-list img { width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 6px; }\n  .book-list h3 { margin: 10px 0 4px; font-size: 18px; }\n  .book-list p { margin: 0; font-size: 14px; opacity: .75; }\n</style>\n\n<script type=\"module\">\n  // WordPress prints the REST API's address in every page's <head>; using it means the\n  // script works on any domain, and on sites installed in a subfolder.\n  const api = document.querySelector('link[rel=\"https://api.w.org/\"]').href;\n  const list = document.getElementById('book-list');\n\n  // Text from the API goes in with textContent, never as HTML.\n  const el = (tag, props = {}) => Object.assign(document.createElement(tag), props);\n\n  try {\n    const res = await fetch(`${api}wp/v2/book?_fields=id,type,title,link,unysonplus_fields&per_page=12`);\n    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`WordPress returned ${res.status}`);\n    const books = await res.json();\n\n    list.replaceChildren(...books.map((book) => {\n      const f = book.unysonplus_fields;\n      const card = el('a', { href: book.link });\n      if (f.cover_image?.url) card.append(el('img', { src: f.cover_image.url, alt: '' }));\n      card.append(\n        el('h3', { textContent: new DOMParser().parseFromString(book.title.rendered, 'text/html').body.textContent }),\n        el('p', { textContent: [f.book_author, f.pages && `${f.pages} pages`].filter(Boolean).join(' · ') }),\n      );\n      return card;\n    }));\n  } catch (error) {\n    list.textContent = `Could not load the books: ${error.message}`;\n  }\n</script>",
      "note": "Paste into a Code Block element with Render as code off. The list, its styles and the script that fills it from the site's own REST API.",
      "highlight": "3,16,23"
    }
  ]
}
